 turnover rate. Fluctuations in environmental iodine levels reflect instantly in neonatal TSH spikes. A high prevalence acts as the most sensitive early clinical warning sign that an environment lacks the iodine required to protect against endemic brain damage. So option B.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 16:19:00.269209+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 18, "fields": {"id": 18, "question": 6751, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "question spacing", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 16:10:54.877756+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 17, "fields": {"id": 17, "question": 5552, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "numbering", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 16:09:18.850803+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 16, "fields": {"id": 16, "question": 6750, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "option words are in the question", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 16:04:52.274214+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 15, "fields": {"id": 15, "question": 6750, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "Their ducts open at the junction of the anterior two-thirds and posterior one-third of the vaginal orifice (hymen), not between anterior one-third and posterior two-thirds. so answer is B.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 16:04:15.765261+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 14, "fields": {"id": 14, "question": 5208, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "numbering", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 15:44:12.691244+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 12, "fields": {"id": 12, "question": 4484, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "numbering", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 15:36:58.867673+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 11, "fields": {"id": 11, "question": 5549, "user": 55, "category": "typo", "comment": "numbering", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 15:36:42.573019+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 9, "fields": {"id": 9, "question": 2026, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "Autosomal recessive trait of a mutation in the gene for UDP-glucuronyl transferase enzyme - This statement is correct. Gilbert Syndrome is indeed characterized by a mutation in the UDP-glucuronyltransferase 1A1 (UGT1A1) gene, which is inherited in an autosomal recessive pattern. so answer is C.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 13:43:44.229000+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 8, "fields": {"id": 8, "question": 2017, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "Given these parameters, the most likely diagnosis is B. Myxedema. Myxedema, associated with hypothyroidism, can cause a transudative pleural effusion, which is characterized by low protein levels in the pleural fluid, as seen here (0.5 g/dL). The low pleural fluid protein level is key in differentiating transudative from exudative effusions.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 07:32:52.273000+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 7, "fields": {"id": 7, "question": 2011, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "Answer is not 'Breathe, Ready, Aim, Fire, Hold' as in A. It's 'Ready, Breathe, Aim, Fire, Hold' as in C.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 07:16:39.498000+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 6, "fields": {"id": 6, "question": 2009, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "The correct statement is C: OS moves closer to the second sound S2 as the stenosis becomes more severe. As severe stenosis to higher LA pressure to earlier valve opening to S2-OS interval shortens.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-18 07:03:53.060000+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 5, "fields": {"id": 5, "question": 6677, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "The pharmacologic effect of Warfarin is likely to Decrease (Option B) when antitubercular treatment (ATT) is started d/t Rifampicin is potent inducer of CYP450.", "status": "new", "is_resolved": false, "resolution_note": "", "resolved_by": null, "resolved_at": null, "notified_user": false, "created_at": "2026-07-17 16:31:12.222000+00:00"}}, {"model": "questions.QuestionFeedback", "pk": 4, "fields": {"id": 4, "question": 6678, "user": 55, "category": "wrong_answer", "comment": "Retrograde amnesia is not a component of Wernicke's syndrome. Wernicke's syndrome is characterized by the classic triad of ataxia ophthalmoplegia, and encephalopathy", "status": "new", "is_resolved": fal